::ALG2_U01_L02_Q01::
Question ID: ALG2_U01_L02_Q01
MLA Standard: MLA.A2.AE.2; MLA.A2.AE.4
Question:
Simplify (4x² + 3x - 8) + (2x² - 5x + 1).
{
~A. 6x² + 8x - 7 #This adds 3x and 5x instead of combining 3x and -5x.
=B. 6x² - 2x - 7 #Correct. Combine like terms: 4x squared plus 2x squared, 3x minus 5x, and -8 plus 1.
~C. 8x² - 2x - 7 #This multiplies the x squared coefficients instead of adding them.
~D. 6x² - 2x + 9 #This adds the constants incorrectly.
}


::ALG2_U01_L02_Q02::
Question ID: ALG2_U01_L02_Q02
MLA Standard: MLA.A2.AE.2; MLA.A2.AE.4
Question:
Simplify (7x³ - 2x + 4) + (-3x³ + 5x - 9).
{
~A. 10x³ + 3x - 5 #This adds 7x cubed and 3x cubed instead of using -3x cubed.
~B. 4x⁶ + 3x - 5 #This incorrectly adds exponents when adding like terms.
~C. 4x³ - 7x - 5 #This combines the x terms incorrectly.
=D. 4x³ + 3x - 5 #Correct. 7x cubed minus 3x cubed is 4x cubed, -2x plus 5x is 3x, and 4 minus 9 is -5.
}


::ALG2_U01_L02_Q03::
Question ID: ALG2_U01_L02_Q03
MLA Standard: MLA.A2.AE.2; MLA.A2.AE.4
Question:
Simplify (5x² - 4x + 6) - (2x² + x - 3).
{
=A. 3x² - 5x + 9 #Correct. Subtract every term in the second polynomial, then combine like terms.
~B. 3x² - 3x + 3 #This does not distribute the subtraction sign to every term in the second polynomial.
~C. 7x² - 5x + 9 #This adds the x squared terms instead of subtracting.
~D. 3x² + 5x + 9 #The x-term sign is incorrect.
}


::ALG2_U01_L02_Q04::
Question ID: ALG2_U01_L02_Q04
MLA Standard: MLA.A2.AE.2; MLA.A2.AE.4
Question:
Simplify (8x² + 3x - 1) - (x² - 6x + 5).
{
~A. 7x² - 3x - 6 #This does not change the sign of -6x when subtracting.
~B. 9x² + 9x - 6 #This adds x squared instead of subtracting it.
=C. 7x² + 9x - 6 #Correct. Distribute the subtraction sign to get -x squared + 6x - 5, then combine.
~D. 7x² + 9x + 4 #This does not subtract the constant 5 correctly.
}


::ALG2_U01_L02_Q05::
Question ID: ALG2_U01_L02_Q05
MLA Standard: MLA.A2.AE.2; MLA.A2.AE.4
Question:
Simplify 4x(3x² - 2x + 7).
{
=A. 12x³ - 8x² + 28x #Correct. Distribute 4x to each term.
~B. 12x² - 8x + 28 #This does not add the exponent from the outside x.
~C. 12x³ - 2x² + 7x #This does not multiply every coefficient by 4.
~D. 12x³ + 8x² + 28x #The middle term should be negative.
}


::ALG2_U01_L02_Q06::
Question ID: ALG2_U01_L02_Q06
MLA Standard: MLA.A2.AE.2; MLA.A2.AE.4
Question:
Simplify -2x(5x² - 3x + 4).
{
~A. -10x² + 6x - 8 #This does not add the exponent from the outside x.
~B. -10x³ - 6x² - 8x #The middle term should be positive because a negative times a negative is positive.
~C. 10x³ - 6x² + 8x #This ignores the negative sign on -2x.
=D. -10x³ + 6x² - 8x #Correct. Multiply each term by -2x.
}


::ALG2_U01_L02_Q07::
Question ID: ALG2_U01_L02_Q07
MLA Standard: MLA.A2.AE.2; MLA.A2.AE.4
Question:
Simplify (x + 7)(x + 2).
{
~A. x² + 14 #This multiplies only the first and last terms.
=B. x² + 9x + 14 #Correct. The middle terms are 2x and 7x, which combine to 9x.
~C. x² + 5x + 14 #The middle terms were subtracted instead of added.
~D. x² + 14x + 9 #The constant and middle coefficient are switched.
}


::ALG2_U01_L02_Q08::
Question ID: ALG2_U01_L02_Q08
MLA Standard: MLA.A2.AE.2; MLA.A2.AE.4
Question:
Simplify (x - 5)(x + 3).
{
~A. x² - 15 #This misses the middle products.
~B. x² + 8x - 15 #This treats -5x as +5x.
=C. x² - 2x - 15 #Correct. x squared + 3x - 5x - 15 combines to x squared - 2x - 15.
~D. x² + 2x - 15 #The middle term sign is incorrect.
}


::ALG2_U01_L02_Q09::
Question ID: ALG2_U01_L02_Q09
MLA Standard: MLA.A2.AE.2; MLA.A2.AE.4
Question:
Simplify (2x + 1)(x + 6).
{
~A. 2x² + 12x + 6 #This misses the 1 times x product.
~B. 2x² + 7x + 6 #This adds 6x and x instead of 12x and x.
~C. 2x² + 13x + 7 #The constant should be 1 times 6, which is 6.
=D. 2x² + 13x + 6 #Correct. 2x times x is 2x squared, 2x times 6 is 12x, and 1 times x is x.
}


::ALG2_U01_L02_Q10::
Question ID: ALG2_U01_L02_Q10
MLA Standard: MLA.A2.AE.2; MLA.A2.AE.4
Question:
Simplify (3x - 4)(x - 2).
{
=A. 3x² - 10x + 8 #Correct. 3x squared - 6x - 4x + 8 combines to 3x squared - 10x + 8.
~B. 3x² - 6x + 8 #This misses the -4x product.
~C. 3x² + 10x + 8 #The middle terms should be negative.
~D. 3x² - 2x + 8 #The middle terms were combined incorrectly.
}


::ALG2_U01_L02_Q11::
Question ID: ALG2_U01_L02_Q11
MLA Standard: MLA.A2.AE.2; MLA.A2.AE.4
Question:
Which pair of terms are like terms?
{
~A. 3x² and 3x #The exponents on x are different.
~B. 7x and 7y #The variables are different.
=C. -5x³ and 8x³ #Correct. Both terms have x raised to the third power.
~D. 4 and 4x #One term has a variable and the other does not.
}


::ALG2_U01_L02_Q12::
Question ID: ALG2_U01_L02_Q12
MLA Standard: MLA.A2.AE.2; MLA.A2.AE.4
Question:
What is the degree of 6x⁴ - 2x² + 9?
{
~A. 6 #This is the leading coefficient, not the degree.
=B. 4 #Correct. The highest exponent is 4.
~C. 2 #This is an exponent in the expression, but it is not the highest exponent.
~D. 9 #This is the constant term, not the degree.
}


::ALG2_U01_L02_Q13::
Question ID: ALG2_U01_L02_Q13
MLA Standard: MLA.A2.AE.2; MLA.A2.AE.4
Question:
Which expression is written in standard form?
{
=A. 2x³ - 4x² + x - 8 #Correct. The exponents decrease from 3 to 2 to 1 to 0.
~B. 5 + 2x² - x #Standard form writes terms in descending order by exponent.
~C. x - 3x² + 7 #The x squared term should come before the x term.
~D. 4 - x + x⁴ #The x to the fourth term should come first.
}


::ALG2_U01_L02_Q14::
Question ID: ALG2_U01_L02_Q14
MLA Standard: MLA.A2.AE.2; MLA.A2.AE.4
Question:
A rectangle has length x + 9 and width x + 4. What polynomial represents the area?
{
~A. 2x + 13 #This adds length and width instead of multiplying.
~B. x² + 36 #This misses the middle products.
=C. x² + 13x + 36 #Correct. Area is (x + 9)(x + 4).
~D. x² - 13x + 36 #Both constants are positive, so the middle term should be positive.
}


::ALG2_U01_L02_Q15::
Question ID: ALG2_U01_L02_Q15
MLA Standard: MLA.A2.AE.2; MLA.A2.AE.4
Question:
A rectangle has length 2x + 5 and width x + 3. What polynomial represents the area?
{
~A. 3x + 8 #This adds the side lengths instead of multiplying them.
~B. 2x² + 15 #This multiplies only the first and last terms.
~C. 2x² + 6x + 15 #This misses the 5x product.
=D. 2x² + 11x + 15 #Correct. (2x + 5)(x + 3) \= 2x squared + 6x + 5x + 15.
}


::ALG2_U01_L02_Q16::
Question ID: ALG2_U01_L02_Q16
MLA Standard: MLA.A2.AE.2; MLA.A2.AE.4
Question:
Find the perimeter of a rectangle with length 3x + 2 and width x + 5.
{
~A. 4x + 7 #This adds length and width once, not the full perimeter.
=B. 8x + 14 #Correct. Perimeter is 2(3x + 2) + 2(x + 5) \= 8x + 14.
~C. 6x + 4 #This doubles only the length.
~D. 6x² + 19x + 10 #This is an area expression, not perimeter.
}


::ALG2_U01_L02_Q17::
Question ID: ALG2_U01_L02_Q17
MLA Standard: MLA.A2.AE.2; MLA.A2.AE.4
Question:
Which expression is equivalent to (x + 4)(x + 4)?
{
~A. x² + 16 #This misses the two middle products.
~B. x² + 8 #This adds the constants but does not multiply the binomials.
=C. x² + 8x + 16 #Correct. (x + 4)(x + 4) \= x squared + 4x + 4x + 16.
~D. x² - 8x + 16 #The middle term should be positive.
}


::ALG2_U01_L02_Q18::
Question ID: ALG2_U01_L02_Q18
MLA Standard: MLA.A2.AE.2; MLA.A2.AE.4
Question:
Which expression is equivalent to (x - 3)²?
{
=A. x² - 6x + 9 #Correct. (x - 3)(x - 3) gives x squared - 6x + 9.
~B. x² - 9 #This misses the middle term.
~C. x² + 6x + 9 #This has the middle term sign wrong.
~D. x² - 3x + 9 #This includes only one middle product.
}


::ALG2_U01_L02_Q19::
Question ID: ALG2_U01_L02_Q19
MLA Standard: MLA.A2.AE.2; MLA.A2.AE.4
Question:
Simplify (x + 5)(x - 5).
{
~A. x² + 25 #The last product is negative because 5 times -5 is -25.
=B. x² - 25 #Correct. The middle terms -5x and 5x cancel.
~C. x² - 10x - 25 #The middle terms should cancel.
~D. x² + 10x - 25 #The middle terms should cancel.
}


::ALG2_U01_L02_Q20::
Question ID: ALG2_U01_L02_Q20
MLA Standard: MLA.A2.AE.2; MLA.A2.AE.4
Question:
Simplify (2x + 3)(2x - 3).
{
~A. 4x² + 9 #The last product is negative because 3 times -3 is -9.
~B. 4x² - 12x - 9 #The middle terms should cancel.
~C. 2x² - 9 #2x times 2x is 4x squared, not 2x squared.
=D. 4x² - 9 #Correct. The middle terms -6x and 6x cancel.
}

